WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
Here are two numbers from
the UK's official forecast

2
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.280
for the year 2026 to 27.

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:11.850
The government expects to
spend 1,449 billion pounds.

4
00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:16.410
It expects to collect 1,316 billion.

5
00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:20.540
That leaves a gap of 133 billion pounds.

6
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.290
So where does a government's
money come from,

7
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:26.610
and what happens when it
spends more than it collects?

8
00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.670
In this mission, you'll
sort taxes into types,

9
00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:33.270
and see which take a bigger
share from poorer households.

10
00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:35.600
Then you'll calculate a budget balance,

11
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.830
and weigh up when a gap
like that is worth running.

12
00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:41.890
Your mission: find out
who pays for government,

13
00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.040
and what a gap like that leads to.
